Z||000004||theogre||12-02-1999||11:07 PM||||someone makes the vet style kit, Pisa I think. It's ugly as far as I'm concerned. Uglier yet since vet is part of why Fiero was scragged.<P>I think "window film" could be used on the tail lamp covers. you want to use a non reflective film. Apply the film to the inside of the cover.<P>You could also dye the covers.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||12-02-1999||11:50 PM||||VHT makes a spray called "The Shadow" made for painting tail/marker lights. Looks black until light is on. I used it on my 73 Camaro and it looked pretty good but I dont know if the paint is still available.||||reg||1
Z||000006||SloPonti||12-03-1999||12:01 AM||||I am very interested in the black tail light covers! go ahead and make them tom!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||14
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-03-1999||12:03 AM||||Be careful putting any permanent blackout on your tail lites.  Many states are getting very strict about that kind of stuff.  If you have the GTS style covers, at least you can remove them if you are stopped.  It's a $50 fine in the town I live in and they do inforce it.  If anybody does blackout their tail lites, PLEASE make sure you have fresh, bright bulbs and keep the indide as well as the outside clean!!!  I've seen many wrecks because of that kind of thing.  And, Tom, if you do decide to produce the GTS style--I want a set.  (For a notchback, please)||||reg||1
Z||000008||DXR_DAD||12-03-1999||12:05 AM||||I have yet to see a nice looking set of after market tail lights for the fiero. The Pisa set... I must agree with Orge, Ugly. So I thought that the stock look with a little tint would look nice. <P>How many fieros do you see with after market tail lights?? and the price, way up there.||||reg||1
