Z||000011||Phil||12-03-1999||08:22 AM||||Well it's different strokes time again. I like the Pisa euro look notchback lights but then again I don't like red cars. Another alternative is to take your lenses apart and apply a couple layers of tint material inside  but cut some holes in it. The effect would be similar to RS Motorsports design. Also very easy to return to original. <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/tail.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/tail.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||ChadMan||12-03-1999||09:18 AM||||There was a guy at the Nationals this year with a beautiful red SE with blacked-out taillamps.  He said he used a spray to do it.  They did look cool, but he turned his lights on, and they were only about half as bright as stock.<P>I'd only be interested if there were a way to do it without diminishing the brightness of the taillamps.||||reg||1
Z||000013||ggarsk||12-03-1999||10:26 AM||||I see that they have halogen backup light bulbs now,so maybe they have them for tailights. I think the only problem there would be heat. i don't think I'd like to melt my lenses or start a fire.||||reg||1
Z||000014||88 Fiero||12-03-1999||02:01 PM||||I have the PISA taillights on my '88 fastback..the first time I got them..they look like shit!!!. I modify to incorporate the stock screws that holds the lenses and by using with one red tailight and one red taillight with a backup light..it turns out great...I modify the wiring so I could use the lense with the backup light...I made that use as a signal and backup...the red lense is for driving lights and stop light....||||reg||1
Z||000015||batboy||12-03-1999||03:38 PM||||Here is a pic of 88 Fieros car to show you what he's talking about. I'm with Phil, I kind of like the round taillights. Maybe not enough to put them on my own car. But what the heck! I also don't care much for bright red cars anymore. Maybe because of all those speeding tickets I got with a red Opel GT during my youth.<P> <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/rearlite.jpg"> ||||reg||1
